# The one problem fragment for the merged kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle
# domain (see packs/dry-run-publish-pack/templates/
# dry-run-publish-case-study.ttl.tmpl for the Kestrel Toolkit case-study
# rationale). Init holds ONLY the Phase 1 (Release Scope & Identity) entry
# atom (scope-engaged); the goal is ONLY the terminal Phase 6 (Receipt &
# Replay) deliverable atom (1 conjunct — the merged goal stays far inside
# PDDL8_MAX_CONJUNCTS=8 because no other fragment declares a goal). Every
# intermediate phase is forced by the precondition chain
# (scope-complete -> generate-complete -> verify-complete ->
# manufacture-complete -> cleanroom-complete -> dry-run-verified), never by
# goal conjuncts: that is how the 8-constraint budget splits across 6
# phases without ever concentrating in one conjunction.
#
# DRY-RUN-OVERCLAIM FENCE: the goal atom is "dry-run-verified", never
# "published", "crates-io-uploaded", or "release-complete" — per the fence
# disclosed in packs/dry-run-publish-pack/ontology.ttl, this pipeline's
# terminal deliverable is a dry-run evidence bundle for a human release
# manager's go/no-go decision, never a live release and never a claim that
# `cargo publish` (without --dry-run) ran.
@prefix ceng:    <urn:chatman:engine#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

_:artifact
    skos:notation "DRY-RUN-PUBLISH-CYCLE-PROBLEM" ;
    dcterms:description "Full dry-run publish gate cycle problem: from scope-engaged to dry-run-verified through all 6 chained phases."@en ;
    ceng:pddlProblem """
(define (problem kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle-p)
  (:domain kestrel-dry-run-publish-cycle)
  (:objects kestrel)
  (:init (scope-engaged kestrel))
  (:goal (dry-run-verified kestrel)))
""" .
